| component | licence | where it sits | what this kit does with it |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Google model-viewer | Apache-2.0 (repository LICENSE); the bundled file carries a BSD-3-Clause header, Copyright 2017 Google LLC | `portal/model-viewer.min.js` | 3D preview for the mesh tools. Vendored so it never loads from a CDN: the page's own `<script src>` values are all `/static/` |
| three.js | MIT | inside the same bundle | model-viewer's renderer; its example URLs (cdn.jsdelivr.net, discourse.threejs.org) are documentation strings, not fetches |
| fflate | MIT (101arrowz) | inside the same bundle | decompression; credited in the bundle's own banner |
| stable-diffusion.cpp | MIT (leejet) | `tools/sd-cpu/` (21 files, incl. the 35 MB `stable-diffusion.dll`) | the console's own picture engine, launched as `sd-cli.exe` (`src/media_tools.py`) |
| llama.cpp | MIT (ggml-org) | fetched into `engine/` (gitignored) by `scripts/fetch_engine.ps1` | the local brain |
| TripoSR | MIT (VAST-AI-Research) | reached from a virtualenv at a config path | photo-to-mesh (`src/mesh_tools.py`) |
| modly | NOASSERTION — the upstream repository declares no standard licence; this kit links to it and carries no code from it | — | referenced only |
| FilmCraft | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | fetched payload (`utilities/filmcraft/`, gitignored) by `scripts/fetch_filmcraft.ps1` | the video editor the film cards drive |
